{
  "data": {
    "text": "To characterize the interregional functional connectivity within the DMN, we defined 32 nodes of interest according to a prior parcellation (Kernbach et al., 2018), including nodes in dmPFC, vmPFC, PMC, TPJ, MTG, and hippocampus.\n\nWe extracted the mean time course for each node and estimated the individual DMN functional connectivity matrices (32 \u00d7 32) by calculating the pairwise Pearson\u2019s correlation coefficient between nodal time courses.\n\nPrior to the network analysis, we generated individual weighted functional networks by applying a correlation threshold rth of 0.2 to remove the spurious correlations.\n\nWe calculated the global efficiency (Eglob) and local efficiency (Eloc) of the DMN to assess parallel information transfer and fault tolerance within the network."
  },
